        "text": "65"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 397.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "All the colours of the rainbow"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 332.4,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Words and expressions for specific colours"
      },
      {
        "y": 74.4,
        "x0": 490.6,
        "x1": 516.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ginger"
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 353.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "pitch black: intensely black, used about darkness, night, etc."
      },
      {
        "y": 100.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 216.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(pitch is an old word for tar)"
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 317.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "jet black: intensely black, used about hair, eyes, etc."
      },
      {
        "y": 124.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 262.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(jet is a black semi-precious gemstone)"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 195.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "scarlet: very bright red"
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 341,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "crimson: strong deep red crimson"
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 267.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shocking pink: an extremely bright pink"
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 315.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ginger: orangey red, used about hair and animal fur"
      },
      {
        "y": 184,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 289.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "navy: dark blue, used about clothes, not eyes"
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 350.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "turquoise: greenish blue, used about fabrics, paint, sea, etc."
      },
      {
        "y": 208.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 182.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "but not usually eyes"
      },
      {
        "y": 216.2,
        "x0": 464.8,
        "x1": 522.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "shocking pink"
      },
      {
        "y": 220,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 223.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lime: a bright yellowish green"
      },
      {
        "y": 232,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 216.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "beige: a light creamy brown"
      },
      {
        "y": 244,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 365.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "mousy: a light, not very interesting brown, used only about hair"
      },
      {
        "y": 256,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 434.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "chestnut: a deep reddish brown, used about hair and horses scarlet"
      },
      {
        "y": 268,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 317.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "auburn: a red-brown colour, usually used about hair"
      },
      {
        "y": 280,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A number of words for gemstones are also used as colour adjectives, e.g. ruby [deep red], emerald"
      },
      {
        "y": 292,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 494.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "[bright green], amber [yellowy orange], coral [orangey pink], sapphire [deep blue], jade [dark green]."
      },
      {
        "y": 313.3,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 267.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Words for talking about colour"
      },
      {
        "y": 330.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Red, blue and yellow are primary colours; by mixing them together you can make other colours."
      },
      {
        "y": 342.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Pastel colours are pale shades of colour – pink, mauve [pale purple] and pale yellow, for example."
      },
      {
        "y": 354.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Strong colours are the opposite of pastels. Harsh colours are colours that are unpleasantly strong."
      },
      {
        "y": 366.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 516.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Vivid colours are strong, bright colours like scarlet or turquoise. Fluorescent colours are very bright"
      },
      {
        "y": 378.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 521.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "colours which seem to glow in the dark. Electric blues or greens are extremely bright blues or greens."
      },
      {
        "y": 390.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 515.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If white has a tinge of green, there is a very slight shade of green in it. If something is monochrome,"
      },
      {
        "y": 402.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "it uses only one (or shades of one) colour, e.g. black, white and grey. The suffixes -y and -ish show"
      },
      {
        "y": 414.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 367.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "that a colour is partly present, e.g. bluey green, reddish brown."
      },
      {
        "y": 436.2,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 198.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Colour metaphors"
      },
      {
        "y": 453.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 416.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "blue = depression (to feel blue); physical or unskilled (blue-collar workers)"
      },
      {
        "y": 465.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 485.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "red = anger (to see red = to be very angry); danger (red alert, a red flag); special importance"
      },
      {
        "y": 477.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 500,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(All the competitors were given the red-carpet treatment. The day we met will always be a red-"
      },
      {
        "y": 489.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "letter day for me.); communist or very left-wing in politics (People’s views sometimes become less"
      },
      {
        "y": 501.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 190.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "red as they get older.)"
      },
      {
        "y": 513.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 520.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "green = nausea (to look green) (People who are seasick often turn/go green and sometimes vomit.);"
      },
      {
        "y": 525.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 502.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "envy (She turned green with envy when she saw her friend’s new car.); care for the environment"
      },
      {
        "y": 537.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 240.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(green tourism; the Green Party)"
      },
      {
        "y": 549.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "black = depressing or without hope (a black future); anger (to look as black as thunder); illegality"
      },
      {
        "y": 561.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 500.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "or incorrectness (black market, black sheep of the family, black mark) (During the war people"
      },
      {
        "y": 573.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 490.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "bought many goods illegally on the black market. If I don’t finish this report in time, that’ll be"
      },
      {
        "y": 585.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 485.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "another black mark against my name. My brother was the black sheep of the family, leaving"
      },
      {
        "y": 598.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 288.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "school and home at the earliest opportunity.)"
      },
      {
        "y": 609.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 377.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "grey = lack of clarity (a grey area); brains (grey matter, grey cells)"
      },
      {
        "y": 621.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 508.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "white = purity (white as snow, whiter than white); being pale (She was so shocked that she went"
      },
      {
        "y": 633.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 492.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "white as a sheet.); a white-knuckle [terrifying] ride at an amusement park such as Disneyland;"
      },
      {
        "y": 645.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 257.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "office workers (white-collar workers)"
      }
    ],
